{"id":"84","method":"turn/start","params":{"approvalPolicy":"never","cwd":"/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-rerun-ef9528d/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.56izx2/repo","input":[{"text":"work-leaf command result\ncommand: grep -n 'struct WorkLeafController\\|impl<B> WorkLeafController\\|fn drain_worker_events\\|review\\|Ready\\|AgentStatusUpdated\\|WorkerEvent::\\|CommandChatResult' /tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-rerun-ef9528d/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.56izx2/context-bundles/orchestrator-1803-0/bundle-2.md\nstatus: 0\nlocked paths: Cargo.toml\nnext: Reply with the next Work Leaf directive, such as `@work-leaf done`, `@work-leaf edit`, `@work-leaf read`, or another `@work-leaf locks run`. Keep any non-directive explanation brief.\nstdout:\n51:- `orchestrator`, `patch`, `review`, `linearize`, and `locks` define core workflow behavior.\n62:- Command orchestration: `CommandChat`, `CommandChatResult`, `ProcessCommand`, `CliError`.\n76:2. Core workflows live in `src/cli.rs`, `src/orchestrator.rs`, `src/patch.rs`, `src/review.rs`,\n185:- orchestrator, patch, review, and linearizer coordination,\n193:- `CommandChat::handle_line` for processing command lines such as `new`, `chat`, `review`, and\n201:`CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.\n216:- background launch/send/review workers,\n218:- review startup, automatic per-patch-agent review routing, reviewer-session creation, and\n219:  reviewed-commit bookkeeping,\n223:loading state. A user-agent response becomes review-ready only when the orchestrator transcript shows\n227:review readiness. Repository build, test, format, and required-check commands run only through\n238:Review bookkeeping has three scopes. The controller records a launch-time review baseline for each\n239:patch agent, tracks the latest reviewed hash for that patch agent so the same agent head is not\n240:reviewed twice, and asks reviewers to inspect every provisional commit from the active baseline\n241:through the latest patch-agent commit. `CommandChat` also keeps the ordered exact review targets that\n242:completed review during the active instance, and those targets form the linearizer handoff. This lets\n243:one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier\n244:reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.\n248:lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching\n261:- `start_review` to create or resume reviewer sessions for explicit history-wide review and stream\n262:  reviewer output.\n277:`CommandTranscriptLine` carries one new command transcript line. `AgentStatusUpdated` carries\n284:spawning, session naming, review lookup, loading bookkeeping, or orchestrator event routing.\n367:`src/review.rs::GitHistory` reads latest agent commits from repository history, builds cumulative\n368:review targets for a patch agent since a launch or reviewed baseline, and resolves agent metadata\n369:commits by exact hash. `ReviewCoordinator<B>` launches reviewer agents against those review targets\n370:and loops until the reviewer reports no findings or the configured maximum round count is reached.\n371:`CommandChat` resolves reviewer `@work-leaf` directives, such as file reads, before interpreting\n372:reviewer output as findings. `CommandChat` and `WorkLeafController` keep a stable\n373:`review-<agent-id>` reviewer identity for each patch agent and skip latest agent heads that have\n374:already completed review. `AgentCommit`, `ReviewResult`, and `ReviewError` are the public review\n375:workflow types. `WorkLeafController` scopes automatic review after a patch agent reports done to the\n376:patch agent that produced the provisional commit; explicit review commands use the history-wide\n377:review target lookup.\n383:exact commits recorded as reviewed in the current command-chat or controller instance; unrelated\n384:historical agent metadata commits are outside the linearizer scope unless the user explicitly reviews\n385:or adds them in that session. When one patch-agent id completes multiple reviewed commits in one\n386:active instance, each reviewed hash is listed independently for the linearizer.\n460:`tests/reviews.rs`, `tests/linearize.rs`, and `tests/workspace.rs` provide the current coverage\n1594:    if agent.id.as_str().starts_with(\"review-\") {\n1607:    let row = if id.starts_with(\"review-\") {\n2057:                    .push(\"commands: new [prompt...], review, linearize, quit\".into());\n2059:            \"review\" => self.transcript.push(\"fixture review: no findings\".into()),\n2420:    CliError, CommandChat, CommandChatResult, command_chat_error_text, command_result_text,\n2423:use crate::review::{AgentCommit, GitHistory, ReviewResult};\n2426:pub struct WorkLeafController<B>\n2438:    reviewers: BTreeSet<AgentId>,\n2439:    review_commits_in_progress: BTreeMap<AgentId, String>,\n2440:    reviewed_agent_commits: BTreeMap<AgentId, String>,\n2441:    agent_review_baselines: BTreeMap<AgentId, String>,\n2444:impl<B> WorkLeafController<B>\n2459:            reviewers: BTreeSet::new(),\n2460:            review_commits_in_progress: BTreeMap::new(),\n2461:            reviewed_agent_commits: BTreeMap::new(),\n2462:            agent_review_baselines: BTreeMap::new(),\n2551:            \"review\" => {\n2552:                if let Err(error) = self.start_review() {\n2629:        self.remember_agent_review_baseline(&agent_id);\n2681:                let _ = stream_sender.send(WorkerEvent::Stream {\n2688:                    let _ = sender.send(WorkerEvent::Complete {\n2694:                    let _ = sender.send(WorkerEvent::Error {\n2704:    pub fn start_review(&mut self) -> Result<Vec<AgentId>, CliError> {\n2705:        self.start_review_for_agent(None)\n2708:    fn start_review_for_patch_agent(\n2712:        self.start_review_for_agent(Some(agent_id))\n2715:    fn start_review_for_agent(\n2731:            &self.age